	<Folder>
		<name>China &gt; Miran &gt; Mysterious arrays</name>
		<visibility>0</visibility>
		<description>25 km WSW of Miran. Unclear whether it&apos;s military or scientific.</description>
		<Placemark>
			<name>China - Miran 1 - Underground power cables?</name>
			<visibility>0</visibility>
			<description>There are no aboveground power lines leadin to this array. I suspect that this thin line (the one that makes a 90 degree turn here and heads southwest) is a buried power (and data?) cable.

Not bookmarked, because it&apos;s too far away from this location: In one of the photos, which obviously has a different date than the others, there is a freshly dug line, though not aways perfectly straight, parallel to the road from Ronqiang (soutwest of here). I suspect that&apos;s where the powerline comes from. It turns north to follow the road to the Miran 3 array but disappears in the Miran 3 photo.</description>
			<LookAt>
				<longitude>88.65096982465202</longitude>
				<latitude>39.16643487656466</latitude>
				<altitude>0</altitude>
				<range>383.6425298078181</range>
				<tilt>0</tilt>
				<heading>0.1426346861779806</heading>
			</LookAt>
			<Style>
				<IconStyle>
					<scale>1.1</scale>
					<Icon>
						<href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/pal4/icon24.png</href>
					</Icon>
				</IconStyle>
				<LabelStyle>
					<scale>1.1</scale>
				</LabelStyle>
			</Style>
			<Point>
				<coordinates>88.65117327146842,39.1668016451377,0</coordinates>
			</Point>
		</Placemark>
